caption: Counteragents and Formula Interactions
technology-rule: counteragents-and-formula-interactions

A formula may name a specific antagonist, purge agent, deactivation signal, treatment, or other early-termination method. The counteragent is built and priced separately. It does not reduce the original formula’s DPL unless susceptibility to it is explicitly taken as a limitation.

A formula may explicitly modify the duration, clearance, addiction, overdose behavior, or effects of another named formula. Such interactions are special properties of the involved formulas; shared ingredients, brand families, or simultaneous use create no automatic interaction.
